      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 11:18 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1495",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4c57465b45dcff133be65dc9c50bf7a6f86e63bb0fb5da1866fe4671f562e74c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4c57465b45dc-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. KNEEDLER: Justice Stevens, and may it please the Court: Respondent alleges in this Bivens action that petitioners, who were postal inspectors, caused him to be prosecuted in retaliation for activity protected by the First Amendment. In order to make out such a claim, however, respondent must establish that there was no probable cause for the prosecution."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondent",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1495",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4c57465b45dcff133be65dc9c50bf7a6f86e63bb0fb5da1866fe4671f562e74c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4c57465b45dc-0000-0002",
      "kind": "allegation",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Respondent alleges in this Bivens action that petitioners, who were postal inspectors, caused him to be prosecuted in retaliation for activity protected by the First Amendment."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1495",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4c57465b45dcff133be65dc9c50bf7a6f86e63bb0fb5da1866fe4671f562e74c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4c57465b45dc-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOUTER: I'm -- I'm not sure why -- why we should make the classification that you did, that -- that retaliatory is simply a species of -- of malicious."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1495",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "4c57465b45dcff133be65dc9c50bf7a6f86e63bb0fb5da1866fe4671f562e74c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4c57465b45dc-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: I would like you to limit yourself to what I didn't concede. I concede it's his company. I concede that he tore some pages out of his notebook, and I concede that he told -- which he did a lot of times. And I concede that he told witnesses answer the question, et cetera. Now, is there anything else connecting him, not his company?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Kneedler",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1495",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "4c57465b45dcff133be65dc9c50bf7a6f86e63bb0fb5da1866fe4671f562e74c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4c57465b45dc-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. KNEEDLER: -- the -- it isn't all about other people. The -- the -- that crime included -- and it's accepted in this case that the Postal Service board of -- board member accepted 30 percent of the fees paid by respondent's company to the consulting firm. Respondent's company. He was the chief executive officer."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court Record",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1495",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "4c57465b45dcff133be65dc9c50bf7a6f86e63bb0fb5da1866fe4671f562e74c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4c57465b45dc-0001-0002",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "board member accepted 30 percent of the fees paid by respondent's company to the consulting firm."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1495",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "4c57465b45dcff133be65dc9c50bf7a6f86e63bb0fb5da1866fe4671f562e74c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4c57465b45dc-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: But because the other side is arguing that even if there is probable cause, the burden shifts when they prove the retaliatory motive,"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1495",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4c57465b45dcff133be65dc9c50bf7a6f86e63bb0fb5da1866fe4671f562e74c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4c57465b45dc-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: Mr. McCartan, I -- I still don't entirely understand what you would want the Government to prove under your system in order to -- in order to -- to win this case. They would have to prove what? That -- that --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. McCartan",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1495",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4c57465b45dcff133be65dc9c50bf7a6f86e63bb0fb5da1866fe4671f562e74c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4c57465b45dc-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "They would have to prove that something other than hostility to protected speech was the reason for the prosecution being advanced."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1495",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4c57465b45dcff133be65dc9c50bf7a6f86e63bb0fb5da1866fe4671f562e74c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4c57465b45dc-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOUTER: Well, they did, but wouldn't you have to prove under your standard not that they would have procured or tried to procure it anyway, but that in fact the prosecutor would have prosecuted anyway? In other words, that's the distinction between the -- the normal case and -- and the case that we're dealing with here --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1495",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4c57465b45dcff133be65dc9c50bf7a6f86e63bb0fb5da1866fe4671f562e74c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4c57465b45dc-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: And -- and were those cases in which the prosecution itself was brought to a halt, or were they post-prosecution damage actions?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice KENNEDY",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1495",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4c57465b45dcff133be65dc9c50bf7a6f86e63bb0fb5da1866fe4671f562e74c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4c57465b45dc-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, but -- but I'm not sure that that proposition has been established in the cases."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. McCARTAN",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1495",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4c57465b45dcff133be65dc9c50bf7a6f86e63bb0fb5da1866fe4671f562e74c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4c57465b45dc-0003-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "No. I think that is the difference, Your Honor, between absolute and qualified immunity. The Court has given absolute immunity only to those functions that are so intimately associated with the judicial process, that they have to give immunity to those people, otherwise there would be an"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. McCARTAN",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1495",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4c57465b45dcff133be65dc9c50bf7a6f86e63bb0fb5da1866fe4671f562e74c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4c57465b45dc-0003-0006",
      "kind": "allegation",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But as Justice Souter brought -- questioned whether the prosecution was procured for unconstitutional reasons, the immunity of the prosecutor has nothing to do with the reasons for which the prosecution is brought."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice STEVENS",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1495",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4c57465b45dcff133be65dc9c50bf7a6f86e63bb0fb5da1866fe4671f562e74c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4c57465b45dc-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 59,
        "start": 59
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "May I ask this question?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. KNEEDLER",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1495",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4c57465b45dcff133be65dc9c50bf7a6f86e63bb0fb5da1866fe4671f562e74c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4c57465b45dc-0003-0005",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 64,
        "start": 64
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "have on law enforcement generally if police officers operate under the assumption that if the prosecution fails, they will be subject to civil liability, which is exactly what Blackstone said, as this Court quoted in Dinsman v. Wilkes."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1495",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4c57465b45dcff133be65dc9c50bf7a6f86e63bb0fb5da1866fe4671f562e74c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4c57465b45dc-0003-0007",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 66,
        "start": 66
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    }
  ],
  "schema_version": "1.0.0"
}
